Z||000000||KitKar||08-26-2000||01:51 AM||||I want to do an engine conversion. But I can't seem to decide which one. My budget is extremely limited.<BR>I have the opportunity to get an almost new 3800 series II for a good price. I just have to have it shipped to me. It seems to me it shouldn't take too much to install but I keep hearing people talking about it costing 3 or $4,000.<BR>So I thought why not just get a cheap, medium mileage 86 or newer carbed 350? I could have it rebuilt and ad TPI in a year or two. Archies basic kit is only $900 or something like that. But again, everyone says 3 or $4,000.<BR>Then I think, longitudinal conversion. A little more difficult but you are supposed to be able to do it for $500 - $1000. Everyone says it will be more. Plus I would have to convert my 5-speed to an Auto.<BR>I am limited to $1,000 - $2,000 for the conversion. What should I do?<P>------------------<BR>Rick Lord<BR>Webmaster<BR>http://www.KitKar.com||||reg||1
